{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media","id":1015514,"title":"Scion Media","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-10T20:43:54-08:00","id":1015514,"title":"Scion Media","content":"In light of the Teotl preview I've been rereading the Obsidian and Blood book series. Which, if you don't know it offhand, is a trio of novels set in a mythic version of Tenochtitlan where a lot of things you'd recognize from Scion are present. The world as it was historically, but just underneath are actual monsters and foolish people playing with magic, and the gods as a real an actual force in the world including investing 'agents' with their own power to serve as earthly actors, not unlike some varieties of Scion.<br /> <br /> Now needless to say it is also pretty strongly its own thing which I'm just drawing parallels with. This world is a bit darker than the world of Scion as we know it, with the gods being far more capricious and frankly hostile than we'd associate with non-titans, historical accuracy is deliberately altered at some points to serve the needs of a story, but still I find it is a pretty good mood setting read.<br /> <br /> So I'm going to float the question out for the forum, what other books or movies or comics or TV do you like to go to when in a mood for something occupying this same niche of myth meshing with reality as we know it? What is your favorite 'Oh man, this would be so great as a game' series? A lot of the influences on both 1e and 2e are pretty known (American Gods, The Wicked + Divine, a bit of Journey Into Mystery, etc) but what do you find clicks best for you? And of course, people feel free to argue or ask questions about anything in here, since in the end this kind of amounts to a media recommendation topic as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T21:39:58-08:00","id":1015534,"title":"","content":"Rick Riordan's entire works deserve honorable mention.<br /> <br /> \u200bHis books pretty much ARE Scion adventures in every way that matters. Heck, the Red Pyramid series may even have good inspiration for a story featuring mortal sorcerers, depending on how they actually look by the time Scion is complete. He does a great job blending the ancient and the modern into a modern myth setting. He's not afraid to be kind of irreverent, either, and the humor in the books is fantastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T21:42:28-08:00","id":1015536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1015534#post1015534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rick Riordan's entire works deserve honorable mention.<br /> <br /> \u200bHis books pretty much ARE Scion adventures in every way that matters. Heck, the Red Pyramid series may even have good inspiration for a story featuring mortal sorcerers, depending on how they actually look by the time Scion is complete. He does a great job blending the ancient and the modern into a modern myth setting. He's not afraid to be kind of irreverent, either, and the humor in the books is fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I've been describing those books as &quot;Scion for Young Readers&quot; for years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T21:46:22-08:00","id":1015539,"title":"","content":"Oh, this is a good question. I don't know if I have any that are strictly similar to Scion, but I have a few that have been exceptionally influential in my depiction of things in Scion.<br /> <br /> The first is Terry Pratchett's Small Gods, which is essentially actually a treatise on the nature of belief, the effect of organized religious systems, and <i>why</i> the world of Scion works. One of the big issues with Scion from a logic perspective is the Gods have withdrawn (to some degree) from the world. The idea that the world continued to function without the Gods, and their cult worship has confused some people, and I always point to Small Gods to address it.<br /> <br /> Small Gods has an analogy of Gods being like a sort of shelled animal. At the core, there is the God. And then that God begins to surround themselves with oracles, prophets, rituals, ceremonies, temples. They go from being a small flicker of a thing to absorbing other Gods, growing huge, the layers the God builds around them grow, and grow. Ritualized behavior continues, practices cement, and everything becomes orderly. And... if the God was to vanish, no one would notice. The shell would remain, even if the little creature at the core died. In this way, entire systems of belief continue without even noticing their God has gone missing (unless you're the Hittites), or even if they have died. People begin to believe in the shell, believe in the behavior, the laws, the practices, the church, the system, and not the God any more.<br /> <br /> Then, the second collection of books that I find immensely helpful for Scion are any of Pratchett's books that deal with the Elves. (Lords and Ladies, The Wee Free Men, and I Shall Wear Midnight) I love the Tuatha, and we don't have a bunch of backing for the Sidhe asides from a few scant snippits of folklore that tend not to be super helpful in actually establishing character. Pratchett's Elves are my remedy to this, horrible, beautiful creatures, that rely on convincing you that they are so much better than you. They would smash the world if they thought it would make a pretty noise, and are creatures of mad, arcane politics, described like cats in their grace, cruelty, and ability to make us forget the cruelty. I think the best quote to sum it up is, &quot;We only remembered that elves sang. But we forgot what they sang about.&quot; <br /> <br /> I Shall Wear Midnight also has an extended visit with The King of the Elves who is Cernunnos for all intensive purposes. There is a single scene with him that perfectly encapsulates how horrifically overwhelming it would be to be in the presence of a Fertility God. I haven't had a chance to weave it into my games since Cernunnos is normally grossly under the weather whenever a game starts due to the Theoi breaking everything, but I might pull it up if Freyr ever comes up.<br /> <br /> There are also The Rook Files by Daniel O'Malley which I describe in my head as &quot;nWoD Hunter if WoD's world wasn't so corrupt and inept it shouldn't function.&quot; It's a great way to see the world of Scion from a mortal, or semi-mortal's perspective. There is the implication that Gods and Goddesses may be kicking about as a Titan's daughter is encountered and treated with the care and attention you would expect a State would treat someone of that power. The story focuses more on small scale things, Hero tier essentially, but it's what I imagine a 2e Government would have, a special branch that exists to prevent things from getting out of hand and getting too public, as well as the group responcible for fufilling all of the myriad of ancient pacts a State ends up hauling around with itself. When you made a pact 900 years ago to always put one hundred cattle on that hill for midnight on this specific night, and you can't <i>exactly</i> remember why, you still want to be doing it just in case it was important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T21:57:18-08:00","id":1015542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1015534#post1015534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rick Riordan's entire works deserve honorable mention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to confess, my only experience with Percy Jackson has been the first movie. I don't mind reading YA books (I honestly read a bunch, a family member is a media specialist at a K-5 school and I tend to get called on to check books for suitability for the 5th graders) but somehow never have actually read the Percy Jackson books. Besides a Totally Not Scion Summer Camp and monsters, what's so great in it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T22:04:48-08:00","id":1015544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1015542#post1015542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to confess, my only experience with Percy Jackson has been the first movie. I don't mind reading YA books (I honestly read a bunch, a family member is a media specialist at a K-5 school and I tend to get called on to check books for suitability for the 5th graders) but somehow never have actually read the Percy Jackson books. Besides a Totally Not Scion Summer Camp and monsters, what's so great in it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The books are actually inspired by Scion if I remember correctly. He used to run games of Scion for his children which is where he got his ideas.<br /> <br /> But, beyond that link, it is very much a Scion story. There are Relics, Visitations, politics based off your Divine Parent, a Fateful Aura, that sort of thing. It does have a Masqurade however, which Scion doesn't actually have. I never read the second series of it however, so there may be even more interesting bits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T22:52:52-08:00","id":1015557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1015544#post1015544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The books are actually inspired by Scion if I remember correctly. He used to run games of Scion for his children which is where he got his ideas.<br /> <br /> But, beyond that link, it is very much a Scion story. There are Relics, Visitations, politics based off your Divine Parent, a Fateful Aura, that sort of thing. It does have a Masqurade however, which Scion doesn't actually have. I never read the second series of it however, so there may be even more interesting bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second series -- the &quot;Heroes of Olympus&quot; books -- actually gets into the differences between the gods' Greek and Roman mantles (and the accompanying personality differences), and the way this affects both their interactions with the world and the kinds of training/support their respective sets of &quot;Scions&quot; receive. There's a lot in there that seems like it'll be relevant, or at least interesting, when 2e is published.<br /> <br /> As for other inspirational media, I find the Dresden Files both a hugely enjoyable read and intriguing for the complex supernatural society that exists separate-but-intertwined with mortal civilization. Like the Percy Jackson books, there is a Masquerade in place, but it seems to be far more permeable. The protagonist could easily be either a mortal magician or a Scion (from what I see, Harry seems to demonstrate the Guardian, Sage, and Warrior Callings).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 12-11-2016, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T00:29:45-08:00","id":1015586,"title":"","content":"Like Yukikaze mentioned, the Dresden Files is pretty awesome and I like reading it even if I'm not in a 'Scion mood' - I like reading it all the time, really.<br /> <br /> Something else that I like reading whenever I want some 'Scion in my life' is Everworld, which has all the gods [though only some of them appear] having left our world and entered a new one [the titular Everworld] along with some of their worshippers and a few other mythical figures. Then some outsiders show up and start screwing up everything. It's written almost exactly like the Animorphs series [which make sense, considering they have the same author] so not everyone will like it. Hell, there are parts of it that I don't like - a lot of parts - but for the most part it's pretty good.<br /> <br /> While Marvel is really, really innaccurate they do occasionally give some interesting spins to mythology when it come up. Marvel fanfiction is way more interesting, though. <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/8388624/1/Schaduw-Wereld\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> is my favourite by far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T06:23:19-08:00","id":1015657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1015542#post1015542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to confess, my only experience with Percy Jackson has been the first movie. I don't mind reading YA books (I honestly read a bunch, a family member is a media specialist at a K-5 school and I tend to get called on to check books for suitability for the 5th graders) but somehow never have actually read the Percy Jackson books. Besides a Totally Not Scion Summer Camp and monsters, what's so great in it?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, the movies were crap compared to the books. The second movie tried to combine, like, three books of the first series into one, and it was terrible.<br /> <br /> \u200bOthers have already said some of the stuff that makes the Percy Jackson series great. It's Scion to the bone. Percy and his friends save the world, fight monsters, and interact with their fellow Scions and the gods in fun and interesting ways.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd that's just the tip of the iceberg. Riordan has done other series based on other mythologies. There's the Red Pyramid series, which is based on Egyptian mythology. As I said, it could be a mortal sorcerers book because according to Riordan, the Egyptian gods don't do the whole &quot;Scion&quot; thing. They don't have children with mortals. Instead, the gods merge with mortals who are descended from the blood of the Pharaohs. There is also an order of Egyptian Magicians called &quot;The House of Life&quot; (which was a real thing in history.) They're mortals with magic strong enough to affect the gods and they act almost as a &quot;supernatural police force,&quot; trying to curtail the god's meddling in the world.<br /> <br /> \u200bThen there's &quot;Magnus Chase and the Gods of Asgard,&quot; dealing with Norse mythology. Magnus is a Scion of Freyr who dies and goes to Valhalla. He and his friends go on wacky adventures to try to prevent Ragnarok. Hilarity ensues.<br /> <br /> \u200bBest of all? Recently, Riordan has started to cross his books over with each other. Percy and his girlfriend Annabeth just met the Kane kids: the main characters of the Red Pyramid series. There was this great story where they had to work together, figuring out ways to combine Greek and Egyptian magic in order to defeat a mutual foe. Magnus, it turns out, is actually Annabeth's cousin and she has appeared in both Magnus Chase books. At the end of the second book (the most recent to come out) Annabeth tells Magnus that he'll need Percy's help with one of his missions.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo yeah. Rick Riordan's books are pure Scion in almost every way. He's got all kinds of great ideas that can be good inspiration for a Scion game (or ten.) For me, the biggest draw is his characters. He has a TON of characters in these books, and yet he manages to give them all their own distinct personality types. Percy is nothing like Carter Kane. Magnus Chase is nothing like Percy or Carter. They're all likeable characters with interesting backgrounds, strengths, and weaknesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T10:21:20-08:00","id":1015720,"title":"","content":"I should note that Riordan does his research. I've immersed myself in Egyptian magic for various projects (especially the REvised Clanbook: Setite and Blood Sacrifice: Secrets of Thaumaturgy). When I read the Kane Chronicles, I kept chortling, &quot;I know about that!&quot; whenever people did magic. But none of it feels forced or &quot;scholarly.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:16:25-08:00","id":1015766,"title":"","content":"Mumbo Jumbo by Ishmael Reed. Set during the Jazz Age, it follows two Voodoo priests as they stumble upon a vast conspiracy called The Wallflower Order, an organization of monotheists descended from the Knight Templars who plan on subverting African-American culture by getting rid of dancing and jazz. I'm not kidding.<br /> <br /> Like Scion's 2nd edition, it imagines a secret, syncretic history of the world where gods and supernatural beings influenced history from the sidelines in a mish mash of real and imagined history. It's a great template for a pre-Visitation game focused less on divine grand feats and more on cultural and mythological exploration.<br /> <br /> Oh and yeah Wicked+The Divine is required reading of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11643,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","user":"Corax","date":". 12-12-2016, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T14:46:30-08:00","id":1016256,"title":"","content":"This is the first I've heard of Mumbo Jumbo, that sounds amazing. Also I'm glad I am reading Rick Riordan's stuff now but not before the first time I ran Scion if that makes any sense? I feel like my style as a GM might have been ludicrously different.<br /> <br /> Thank you, thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T17:54:14-08:00","id":1016337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1016256#post1016256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the first I've heard of Mumbo Jumbo, that sounds amazing. Also I'm glad I am reading Rick Riordan's stuff now but not before the first time I ran Scion if that makes any sense? I feel like my style as a GM might have been ludicrously different.<br /> <br /> Thank you, thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I know what you mean about Rick Riordan. His books sound great but I'm afraid reading them will influence me too much, especially since I'm GMing and most of my players knee jerk response to being told about Scion was &quot;so it's like Percy Jackson&quot; and I want to show how versatile the game and setting can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T21:35:47-08:00","id":1016397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1015657#post1015657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBest of all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Best of all is Alex Fierro!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T21:51:54-08:00","id":1016400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1016397#post1016397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Best of all is Alex Fierro!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, she's pretty much my fave in the Magnus Chase series. Such a badass! <br /> <br /> And Alex is a perfect segue into talking about how inclusive Riordan is as a writer. The guy has managed to represent just about every ethnicity on the planet, and I don't think he's had to resort to stereotypes even once to make them work.<br /> <br /> Not just ethnic diversity either. Different sexualities and gender identities as well. The aforementioned Alex &quot;Pure Awesome&quot; Fiero is one of the first gender fluid characters I've ever seen in fiction, and she's easily the best character in the series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:09:50-08:00","id":1017250,"title":"","content":"Also worth mentioning is Disney's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1007565-moana\">Moana</a>. This movie has me wanting the Atua Pantheon SO much!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T16:38:07-08:00","id":1017384,"title":"","content":"The Type Moon universe (or multiverse, technically) is also pretty good for Scion-like stuff. Kind of, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T15:37:14-08:00","id":1018238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1015544#post1015544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The books are actually inspired by Scion if I remember correctly. He used to run games of Scion for his children which is where he got his ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlikely, given that Scion: Hero was published in 2007 while the first Percy Jackson came out in 2005.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T16:03:25-08:00","id":1018247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1018238#post1018238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unlikely, given that Scion: Hero was published in 2007 while the first Percy Jackson came out in 2005.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Apparently I got it wrong. It may have been the second series then, Wikipedia credits his second series to inspiration from Scion and Warcraft, however it is troublingly not cited properly. All of the references to it seem to be uncited as well. I could have <i>sworn</i> I read it either in an interview, or possibly on a photo of the inside sleeve of one of the books. I feel like it was linked on the old White Wolf Forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T22:23:35-08:00","id":1018346,"title":"","content":"Is anyone else here familiar with the <i>The Secret World</i> MMO?<br /> <br /> It doesn't map exactly to <i>Scion</i> (in fact, it's far more akin to what a World of Darkness MMO would be like), but there's quite a bit in it that would be recognizable to <i>Scion</i> players: morally-grey organizations squabbling for supremacy, divinely-empowered human agents as the first and only effective line of defense against horrors out of mythology and science fiction, and godlike beings moving everyone else around like pawns on a chessboard for their own inscrutable reasons. (It even involves Loki and Aten as antagonists at different points in the storyline.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T22:26:07-08:00","id":1018348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1018247#post1018247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah! Apparently I got it wrong. It may have been the second series then, Wikipedia credits his second series to inspiration from Scion and Warcraft, however it is troublingly not cited properly. All of the references to it seem to be uncited as well. I could have <i>sworn</i> I read it either in an interview, or possibly on a photo of the inside sleeve of one of the books. I feel like it was linked on the old White Wolf Forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the timeline doesn't quite work for the original series, but it could well be true for Heroes of Olympus, The Kane Chronicles, and Magnus Chase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T22:39:12-08:00","id":1018351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1018247#post1018247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah! Apparently I got it wrong. It may have been the second series then, Wikipedia credits his second series to inspiration from Scion and Warcraft, however it is troublingly not cited properly. All of the references to it seem to be uncited as well. I could have <i>sworn</i> I read it either in an interview, or possibly on a photo of the inside sleeve of one of the books. I feel like it was linked on the old White Wolf Forms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You might be thinking of the rumors surrounding Avatar the Last Airbender and first edition Exalted. Certain writers are positive it was a direct influence though they acknowledge they can't prove it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T23:33:02-08:00","id":1018360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1018346#post1018346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anyone else here familiar with the <i>The Secret World</i> MMO?<br /> <br /> It doesn't map exactly to <i>Scion</i> (in fact, it's far more akin to what a World of Darkness MMO would be like), but there's quite a bit in it that would be recognizable to <i>Scion</i> players: morally-grey organizations squabbling for supremacy, divinely-empowered human agents as the first and only effective line of defense against horrors out of mythology and science fiction, and godlike beings moving everyone else around like pawns on a chessboard for their own inscrutable reasons. (It even involves Loki and Aten as antagonists at different points in the storyline.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never wrapped up all of the story for The Secret World, I had my money on Soloman Island's magical sword being Nuada's sword made out of light until the reveal. But, it's a really great base for... How would I put it. A Scion setting where Scions are exceptionally rare and Mortals handle pretty much everything. Or perhaps a world right before Scions start being Awoken because things are lapsing into the 'out of hand' territory.<br /> <br /> It's a lot like The Rook series I was previously talking about really, except less globe-spanning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1018351#post1018351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might be thinking of the rumors surrounding Avatar the Last Airbender and first edition Exalted. Certain writers are positive it was a direct influence though they acknowledge they can't prove it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never actually heard of that one, you've set me on something to check out tomorrow! I have, much to my shame, never actually looked at Exalted much. I do love Last Airbender though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T23:44:36-08:00","id":1018362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1018360#post1018360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have never wrapped up all of the story for The Secret World, I had my money on Soloman Island's magical sword being Nuada's sword made out of light until the reveal. But, it's a really great base for... How would I put it. A Scion setting where Scions are exceptionally rare and Mortals handle pretty much everything. Or perhaps a world right before Scions start being Awoken because things are lapsing into the 'out of hand' territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly the kind of setting it is. But the PCs are undeniably Scion level.<br /> <br /> I would definitely recommend finishing the storyline (what has been released so far, anyway). Particularly since (not to give spoilers) there are some cutscenes that seem similar to what advancing from one tier of Scion-hood to the next must be like...<br /> <br /> On a more meta note, if you're involved in the game's RP community (like I am), there are a large number of players RPing not only as the default PC type, but as lycanthropes, mortal magicians, minor or retired deities, all sorts of character concepts. What has been said about <i>Scion: Origins</i> reminds me strongly of that, the wide-open sandbox feel (and when Origins and Hero drop, I'll probably use them for &quot;tabletop&quot; TSW RP).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","user":"yukikaze","date":". 12-17-2016, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T03:07:44-08:00","id":1018396,"title":"","content":"The one that sprung to mind for me was <i>Loki: Agent of Asgard</i>. Marvel's God of Evil gets a fresh start after being reincarnated, and tries to reinvent himself as a hero, only to find that his true nature isn't so easy to escape. It's clever, funny, the mythology is integrated really well with a mystery / heist story, and it's an interesting examination of what a god is, and the limitations they work under.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T04:23:13-08:00","id":1018417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1018346#post1018346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anyone else here familiar with the <i>The Secret World</i> MMO?<br /> <br /> It doesn't map exactly to <i>Scion</i> (in fact, it's far more akin to what a World of Darkness MMO would be like), but there's quite a bit in it that would be recognizable to <i>Scion</i> players: morally-grey organizations squabbling for supremacy, divinely-empowered human agents as the first and only effective line of defense against horrors out of mythology and science fiction, and godlike beings moving everyone else around like pawns on a chessboard for their own inscrutable reasons. (It even involves Loki and Aten as antagonists at different points in the storyline.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I played up through a good chunk of Tokyo but I hate the &quot;force field&quot; mechanics they added there.<br /> <br /> Plus I am unfond of some of the balance decisions made about the training simulations in Venice.<br /> <br /> It should be said that the empowered human agents come back from the dead so reliably a really powerful villain early in the game considers it far too much bother to actually do what it takes to kill one. They're also immortal.<br /> <br /> Of course later on there's technology that interferes with the resurrection power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T20:43:14-08:00","id":1018668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elemental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1018396#post1018396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one that sprung to mind for me was <i>Loki: Agent of Asgard</i>. Marvel's God of Evil gets a fresh start after being reincarnated, and tries to reinvent himself as a hero, only to find that his true nature isn't so easy to escape. It's clever, funny, the mythology is integrated really well with a mystery / heist story, and it's an interesting examination of what a god is, and the limitations they work under.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love a lot of Marvel's stuff with Thor and the Asgardians. It often bears only the most tenuous link to actual myth, but that doesn't stop some arcs from being genuinely good stuff, especially recent Loki stuff exploring the nature of being myths. But also go give Walt Simonson's Thor stuff a read just for great material, totally 'whatever' stance towards myths aside it is gold","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T14:04:50-08:00","id":1021679,"title":"","content":"It's mudane but the TV Outsiders has always reminded me of a group of mortals who came over with some Tuatha and tried to stick to old ways. Really want to make a Scion who comes out of that kind of environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T14:33:22-08:00","id":1022458,"title":"","content":"The October Days series by Seaman McGuire is a great series. The main character is the half-blood child of a tad demigod.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T14:35:36-08:00","id":1022460,"title":"","content":"I have auto spell check, it keeps messing up my posts when I type names in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T20:14:39-08:00","id":1025255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1015766#post1015766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mumbo Jumbo by Ishmael Reed. Set during the Jazz Age, it follows two Voodoo priests as they stumble upon a vast conspiracy called The Wallflower Order, an organization of monotheists descended from the Knight Templars who plan on subverting African-American culture by getting rid of dancing and jazz. I'm not kidding.<br /> <br /> Like Scion's 2nd edition, it imagines a secret, syncretic history of the world where gods and supernatural beings influenced history from the sidelines in a mish mash of real and imagined history. It's a great template for a pre-Visitation game focused less on divine grand feats and more on cultural and mythological exploration.<br /> <br /> Oh and yeah Wicked+The Divine is required reading of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, those were both required reading for Scion 2e's writing staff. Good calls on both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T22:13:34-08:00","id":1025297,"title":"","content":"I feel like the only person who has read Wicked+The Divine and didn't like it. It isn't even hating the author either, I've enjoyed both Big 2 and smaller press stuff he's done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T07:47:11-07:00","id":1094862,"title":"","content":"Well, I have a few things I think about and get inspiration from when considering running a scion game.<br /> <br /> Investiture of the Gods which is a major work in the Shenmo genre of vernacular fiction. The interplay between mortals and immortals is how I easily imagine it working in the World of Scion, but also because my father read it to me as a child from a very old looking copy of the book in Chinese. The story about how king wen of zhou knowingly ate the entrails of his slain son (which my father made even scarier when he told me that our surname was the same as those characters, including the Chinese character) is the most memorable for me because of the high cost of life and morality in order to gain something later on.<br /> <br /> Mahabharata, when the Vedic people claim that all that one need read to understand the nature of existence is this book, I believe them. So many story seeds, especially related to gods, can be found in this work, if one can take the times to read all of the parvas and the various descendants and derivative works. The gambling game, even as the mundane deception that it is, can test the nature of character, the idea of honor, and the understanding of right action.<br /> <br /> 1001 nights. As a collection of stories, the work is useful when attempting to create scenes within a session and making sure to focus on the importance of the plot over the mundane and repetitive elements of day to day living. It also has the added bonus of the heroes of the stories worshiping a monotheistic deity, but still must cope with the idea of interacting with powerful supernatural beings and magical wonders.<br /> <br /> Saint Seiya. This is a more recent work by Masami Kurumada. The work is interesting because it combines Greek, Japanese, and Chinese mythology and concepts. Specifically, the superficial and detail elements are greek, such as the gods, constellations, cosmos, and cloths. But the pillars of the story as well as the metaphysical elements come from the authors own understanding of his own culture. Things such as the various senses, the martial arts, the underlying principles of super moves, and the relationship gods have with the various elements of the world. Without spoiling anything a simple example would be the underworld is called hades, but functions like an Indian, Chinese, or Japanese undeworld rather than a greek one. Anyway, for a scion game that takes all myths to be true, Saint Seiya is a good example of how that can be done combining various cultural elements into a single story. It also helps that it has worldwide popularity and can be name dropped to explain to a new player.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T12:59:12-07:00","id":1094923,"title":"","content":"<i>Mumbo Jumbo</i> is my favorite novel. Everything I write owes something to that book, Scion especially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T16:17:46-07:00","id":1094962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1094862#post1094862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saint Seiya.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://postimg.org/image/t9lfa8ruh/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://s28.postimg.org/imrm4tjp9/SHAKA.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T17:24:25-07:00","id":1094973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1094962#post1094962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.org/image/t9lfa8ruh/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://s28.postimg.org/imrm4tjp9/SHAKA.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An encapsulation of my point. On a side note, I hope the Saint path can be used to emulate this approach because that would be pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Edit: I am referring to syncretic nature of the example for a saint path, but if one could actually be saint in the saint seiya style, that would be even cooler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":1715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","user":"Ostarion","date":". 05-20-2017, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T01:05:29-07:00","id":1095054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1018351#post1018351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might be thinking of the rumors surrounding Avatar the Last Airbender and first edition Exalted. Certain writers are positive it was a direct influence though they acknowledge they can't prove it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the Wikipedia page for the second Rick Riordan series, <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lost_Hero\" target=\"_blank\">The Lost Hero</a></b>. It specifically mentions Warcraft and Scion as inspirations, but doesn't provide any citation. I also seem to recall an interview or something where it gets mentioned, but I have no idea where that might be if I'm not just imagining things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:52:31-07:00","id":1095191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1018668#post1018668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love a lot of Marvel's stuff with Thor and the Asgardians. It often bears only the most tenuous link to actual myth, but that doesn't stop some arcs from being genuinely good stuff, especially recent Loki stuff exploring the nature of being myths. But also go give Walt Simonson's Thor stuff a read just for great material, totally 'whatever' stance towards myths aside it is gold</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll second the Walt Simonson recommendation. You have no idea how thrilled I was to see that Skurge the Executioner will be in the next movie, <i>and</i> will be doing the twin M-16s bit. (The fact that he's being played by Karl Urban only makes this more awesomely awesome.)<br /> <br /> I also rather enjoyed the Incredible Hercules series that followed World War Hulk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:24:22-07:00","id":1095279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UnjustCustos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1021679#post1021679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mudane but the TV Outsiders has always reminded me of a group of mortals who came over with some Tuatha and tried to stick to old ways. Really want to make a Scion who comes out of that kind of environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might consider Alex Bledsoe's &quot;Tufa&quot; novels, which are actually about the descendants of the Tuatha De Danaan and Fomorians after they resettled in Appalachia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/364-logos-invictus","name":"Logos Invictus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T07:32:38-07:00","id":1095470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1015514-scion-media?p=1095191#post1095191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll second the Walt Simonson recommendation. You have no idea how thrilled I was to see that Skurge the Executioner will be in the next movie, <i>and</i> will be doing the twin M-16s bit. (The fact that he's being played by Karl Urban only makes this more awesomely awesome.)</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://i345.photobucket.com/albums/p388/proteus_lives/Scan11819.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">He stood alone at Gjallerbru</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T10:10:41-07:00","id":1095530,"title":"","content":"I didn't see it posted earlier in the thread, but I'd also like to recommend the Gods &amp; Monsters books from Abaddon Books. The first, Unclean Spirits, is written by Chuck Wendig, and the series follows various takes on a modern world where the gods struggle with each other like organized crime families. My favorite in the series thusfar has been Cassandra Khaw's &quot;Rupert Wong, Cannibal Chef&quot;, which involves the ghouls, djinn, Greek furies, and the gods of the Chinese underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},